From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: a Recent shortcut points at its document

Since 1664 SHAddToRecentDocs hands every path to the shortcut step as SHARD_PATHW, which gave the wide path to IShellLinkA::SetPath: every Recent\*.lnk pointed at "C:\C", and Quick access's Recent files, which leaves out links to nothing, stayed empty. SHARD_PATHW goes through IShellLinkW::SetPath.
---
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shellord.c b/dlls/shell32/shellord.c
index af30a20..3a0b952 100644
--- a/dlls/shell32/shellord.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shellord.c
@@ -1178,7 +1178,22 @@ static void SHADD_add_document(UINT uFlags,LPCVOID pv)
 	    /* Set the document path or pidl */
 	    if (uFlags == SHARD_PIDL) {
                 hres = IShellLinkA_SetIDList(psl, pv);
-	    } else {
+	    }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_RECENT_PATH_ANSI
+	    /* Stained Glass OS: SHAddToRecentDocs hands every path on as
+	     * SHARD_PATHW (1664); the wide path given to the ANSI SetPath made
+	     * every Recent link's target "C:\C", and Quick access's Recent files,
+	     * which skips links to nothing, has stayed empty */
+	    else if (uFlags == SHARD_PATHW) {
+                IShellLinkW *pslw;
+                hres = IShellLinkA_QueryInterface(psl, &IID_IShellLinkW, (void **)&pslw);
+                if (SUCCEEDED(hres)) {
+                    hres = IShellLinkW_SetPath(pslw, pv);
+                    IShellLinkW_Release(pslw);
+                }
+	    }
+#endif
+	    else {
                 hres = IShellLinkA_SetPath(psl, pv);
 	    }
 	    if(FAILED(hres)) {
